Push-to-talk dictation in the composers, through this deployment's speech server.

Hold Right ⌥ (or another key, chosen in Settings → Speech), or hold the
mic button next to Send, and talk: the words stream into the draft at the
caret as the speech server recognizes them, each fading in. Letting go
stops the microphone and the stream; the last words arrive and the text
stays in the composer, or is sent if Send when you let go is on. Esc, or
sliding a finger off the button to the left, puts the draft back.

The browser streams 16 kHz PCM straight to the server GET /v1/info names
(push_to_talk_url, server patch 0025-push-to-talk.patch), a Voxtral
Realtime server that transcribes on its own machine, or relays the audio to
Mistral's hosted Voxtral or to Deepgram Nova-3 (lib/pushToTalk.ts). The
socket and the microphone open together, and audio captured before the
server is ready is held for it. A take also ends when the window loses
focus or the tab is hidden (the key-up would never arrive), and after
2 minutes, so nothing streams to a paid service once you've let go.

While a take runs, the composer card says data-ptt-state: its tools give
way to a bar with a recording dot, the time, a live waveform, the model
and how to cancel (pushToTalk.css), and the textarea is read-only. The bar
is no taller than the buttons, so the card keeps its height. It replaces the
tools at once when a take starts; for a moment after one, the card says
"ended" and the bar, pinned where it was, fades out while the tools fade
back in underneath it, so the row is never empty for a frame.
The waveform keeps its bars when listening turns to finishing, so they
trail off to silence instead of blanking when you let go. The
draft is drawn by the composer's highlight backdrop so the words can fade
in; Deepgram's words that may still change are dimmed.

Settings → Speech (components/PushToTalkSettings.tsx) picks the model, the
key, the words to listen for (Mistral's context bias and Deepgram's
keyterms), and what letting go does, and shows whether the server answers.
The choices are kept per browser and are part of Export settings.
Both the session composer and the New session screen have it; the side
chat doesn't.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0039.
